  p1 {"pageIndex":1,"type":10,"rect":{"origin":{"x":308.862,"y":560.7344},"size":{"width":237.9946,"height":80.6375}},"segmentRects":[{"origin":{"x":320.817,"y":560.7344},"size":{"width":224.2924,"height":8.9065}},{"origin":{"x":308.862,"y":572.6894},"size":{"width":237.9035,"height":8.9065}},{"origin":{"x":308.862,"y":584.6444},"size":{"width":236.2507,"height":8.9065}},{"origin":{"x":308.862,"y":594.8992},"size":{"width":235.9506,"height":10.6067}},{"origin":{"x":308.862,"y":608.5544},"size":{"width":236.2517,"height":8.9065}},{"origin":{"x":308.862,"y":618.8092},"size":{"width":236.2492,"height":10.6067}},{"origin":{"x":308.862,"y":632.4654},"size":{"width":237.9946,"height":8.9065}}],"strokeColor":"#007f00","color":"#007f00","opacity":1,"author":"金之盛","contents":"In this section, we provide a trajectory going from a ResNet to a ConvNet that bears a resemblance to Transformers. We consider two model sizes in terms of FLOPs, one is the ResNet-50 / Swin-T regime with FLOPs around 4.5×109 and the other being ResNet-200 / Swin-B regime which has FLOPs around 15.0 × 109. For simplicity, we will present the results with the ResNet-50 / Swin-T complexity models.Tess","modified":"2026-11-20T23:38:53.000Z","flags":["print"],"blendMode":0,"appearanceModes":1}
